---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Is this a remote control for Claude Code?",
    a: "No. rply doesn't mirror sessions or run your agent. Your agent decides when to reach you, and you answer.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need MCP?",
    a: "No. It's a CLI, so any agent with a shell can use it, and so can cron jobs and CI. A remote MCP endpoint for hosted agents is planned.",
  },
  {
    q: "How does push work if I self-host?",
    a: "Your server sends a small relay a wake-up ping with no content. Your phone wakes up and fetches the message straight from your server. No Apple or Google keys needed.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can the server read my messages?",
    a: "If you self-host, it's your server. Optional end-to-end encryption per channel is planned, so not even the server can read it.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does it cost?",
    a: "Self-hosting is free. Pricing for the hosted version comes when it launches.",
  },
];
---

<section class="py-24">
  <h2 class="mb-12 text-center">Fair questions.</h2>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl rounded-[28px] border border-line bg-white">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 border-b border-line px-6 py-4">
      <span
        class="grid size-7 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-linear-to-b from-accent-400 to-accent-500 text-small font-semibold text-white"
        >r</span
      >
      <span class="text-ui font-medium">rply</span>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 p-6">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <>
            <p class="max-w-[80%] self-end rounded-2xl rounded-br-md bg-accent-500 px-4 py-2 text-white">{faq.q}</p>
            <p class="mb-3 max-w-[80%] self-start rounded-2xl rounded-bl-md bg-neutral-100 px-4 py-2">{faq.a}</p>
          </>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
